From: Veron
Subject: [PATCH] stdarg: va_copy's arguments are reversed

    #define va_copy(ap1, ap2) ap2 = ap1

C says va_copy(dest, src) copies SRC INTO DEST. This assigns ap1 into ap2 --
backwards. Correct C therefore does the opposite of what it says:

    va_copy(v, ap);          /* means: v = ap                        */
                             /* does:  ap = v, with v uninitialised  */

so it destroys the live argument pointer AND leaves the copy holding garbage.

HOW THIS SURVIVED. Nothing upstream uses it. Zero uses in M2libc, zero in
M2-Planet's compiler sources. The single use in the whole tree is a test:

    va_start(args, count);
    va_copy(args, second_args);        test/run-pass/variadic_functions.c:57
    ... then reads va_arg(args) and va_arg(second_args) ...

second_args is uninitialised on that line, so as C it is meaningless. The
author meant "copy args into second_args" and wrote the arguments in the same
reversed order the macro expects, so the two errors cancel and the test
passes. It has always passed and it proves nothing.

CONSEQUENCE OF FIXING IT: that test depends on the reversed direction and will
FAIL against this patch. The test is wrong, not the fix -- but a run that
executes M2-Planet's own suite will go red and should not be read as a
regression.

WHY IT MATTERS HERE. tcc uses va_copy in the standard order in cstr_vprintf,
which is on the path of every diagnostic tcc emits:

    va_copy(v, ap);
    len = vsnprintf(cstr->data + cstr->size, size, fmt, v);   tccpp.c:420

The micro-c-built tcc segfaulted inside tcc_set_output_type. The trace was
tccelf_add_crtbegin -> tcc_add_crt("crt1.o") -> tcc_add_library_internal ->
tcc_error_noabort -> error1 -> cstr_vprintf. The crt files genuinely are not
present; tcc was trying to SAY SO and crashed formatting the message, before
reading a line of source.

With this patch the same binary prints

    tcc: error: file 'crt1.o' not found
    tcc: error: file 'crti.o' not found

and the driver advances from marker D2 to D4 -- past tcc_set_output_type and
into tcc_add_file, the compile path, for the first time.

Verified on aarch64 under qemu: va_copy(v, ap) followed by va_arg(v, char*)
segfaults before and returns the right value after, and the full tcc rebuild
above was run end to end.

diff --git a/stdarg.h b/stdarg.h
index 573d800..9bcc379 100644
--- a/stdarg.h
+++ b/stdarg.h
@@ -24,6 +24,6 @@ typedef __va_list va_list;
 #define va_start __va_start
 #define va_arg __va_arg
 #define va_end __va_end
-#define va_copy(ap1, ap2) ap2 = ap1
+#define va_copy(ap1, ap2) ap1 = ap2
 
 #endif
